Start pipa's source storage runtime after vfsinit, behind XNU_PIPA_SOURCE_STORAGE.

UniXNU-sheng's source-storage-runtime.patch makes the same call through a weak import; on this kernel a weak
reference to an absent definition is a chained-fixup import, which XnuPrelink refuses (kernel-build run
42991705340, see zzzz-pipa-macos-absent-features.patch). So the call is strong and compiled only when
XNU_PIPA_SOURCE_STORAGE is set, which pipa_macos26_ufs_defconfig does together with force-loading
libShengSourceStorage.a. pipa_macos26_defconfig does not set it: that kernel is unchanged by this patch.

What the runtime does is decided by devices/pipa/package/PipaStorageGuard.h: nothing unless
native-source-storage=1 and native-ufs-probe is one of the read-only inspections (2, 6, 7, 8); it refuses every
root, store, log and publishing mode, so no root comes from Android's userdata and nothing is written to UFS.

